<!--
v0.72: director feedback — "아마 알림 아이콘도 필요하겟지..?" (this app
will probably need a proper notification icon too). Confirmed: both
DailyReminderReceiver and the new IncidentCheckWorker were reusing
R.mipmap.ic_launcher (a full-color detective-cat illustration) as their
small status-bar icon, which Android forces into a solid white silhouette
of whatever the drawable's bounding shape is — for a busy multi-color
illustration that reads as an unrecognizable white blob, not the launcher
icon in miniature. Android's own notification icon guideline requires a
flat, single-color (alpha-only) silhouette instead.

A paw print was the simplest shape that (a) reads clearly at 24dp status-
bar size, (b) still connects to the app's own cat-detective branding
without trying to cram the full illustration into a silhouette, and
(c) needed no new external asset — built here directly as 5 simple
ellipses (one pad + four toes) rather than traced from artwork, since
notification icons are conventionally this simple anyway (compare any
system app's own ic_stat_* icons). Fill color is left as pure white:
Android's NotificationManager re-tints a notification's small icon to
whatever the current status bar/notification-shade theme expects
(normally white, sometimes an accent color on some OEM skins) and ignores
this drawable's own color for that purpose — white is just the
conventional authoring color so the un-tinted drawable still previews
sensibly (e.g. in Android Studio's resource preview).
-->
